### Verifier: AIT settle legs read through the ledger hash (VERIFY-3)

`check_ait_chain` selected trades `WHERE settlement_ait_tx_hash IS NOT
NULL`, so pre-mirror-fix settled trades (VERIFY-2 heals them only on the
ledger row) were never verified on chain — the live run counted 0 legs.

- `05b5e7351` — with `--bridge-db`, a settled trade whose tape column is
  empty takes `settle_ait_tx_hash` from the settled trade-kind ledger
  row (reusing `_settle_trade_ait_hashes`) and runs the identical
  recipient/value/fee-leg checks. No hash anywhere stays a FAIL from
  the DB check and is skipped in the AIT lane; without `--bridge-db`
  the lane is unchanged. The leg count now reads
  `N settlement AIT legs checked (T from tape, L from ledger)`.
### CLEAN-1: minor residuals — settlement terminal marks, status NaN guard, CLI wallet safety, tooling

- `b2393aa68` — settlement monitor: a `below_fee` inbound lock is now marked terminally (one WARNING, no forever-retry) matching the owner-remainder path, and `_lock_refund_ref_id` fails closed to `None` on an empty/non-hex lock hash — the caller treats it as `duplicate` (operator review) instead of crashing the lane.
- `53cd7ca45` — `website/status.js`: `Date.parse(head.timestamp)` producing `NaN` no longer reaches `fmtAge`; an unparseable or future-skewed head renders `live` without an age claim instead of `stale NaN…`. No test exists — the repo has no JS engine in the test tier and a text-extraction unit test was rejected by the task.
- `34a6365fa` — `genesis init` exits non-zero when `--password*` is given without `--create-wallet` (it printed an error and returned 0). Wallet liquidity stake/unstake re-saves go through `_resave_wallet`: an encrypted wallet can never be written back without the resolved password — `_load_wallet` may resolve one internally that the caller never sees, so a missing `resolved_password` aborts rather than dumping the plaintext key under the `encrypted` flag. The same pattern remains in `wallet/basic.py` (3 sites) — follow-up.
- `983fd1c3c` — `exchange order my --wallet` resolves the address metadata-only via `_fund_wallet_address` (the helper `order fund` already uses): reads the plaintext `address` field of an encrypted wallet file with daemon fallback, never touching key material — the command is documented "address only — no signing" yet demanded a password path (15 Oct D4 live find).
- `5699a1dc7` — tooling: (a) `check-mypy-changed.sh` already honoured `PYTHON` on both paths via `repo-python.sh` since TEST-1 (`af1b2adaa`) — verified, no change. (b) `no_float_money` gains `TIME_TOKENS` (deadlines, timestamps, retry counters, durations) so a `dict[int, float]` of monotonic deadlines under a money-named identifier is no longer a false positive; `at`/`last` deliberately stay guarded (`balance_at`, `last_payment` are amounts), `# not-money:` remains the escape hatch. (c) the exchange contract test's `bridge_monitor` fixture evicts `sys.modules` entries resolved outside the checkout and asserts the import lands under `_REPO_ROOT` — a stale cache from the venv's `aitbc-root.pth` (`/opt/aitbc` on `sys.path`) would otherwise silently win the `sys.path` insert and monkeypatch would pin nothing.

